.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt ZPOOL-REPARITY 8
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm zpool-reparity
.Nd reshape the RAIDZ parity level of a ZFS storage pool in place
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm zpool
.Cm reparity
.Op Fl -online | Fl -async | Fl -status | Fl -cancel
.Op Fl -target Ar N
.Ar pool
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Increases (promotes) the parity level of the RAIDZ top-level virtual devices of
.Ar pool
in place \(em
.Sy raidz1 Ns \(->\| Ns Sy raidz2
or
.Sy raidz2 Ns \(->\| Ns Sy raidz3 Ns
\(em without adding devices, without send/receive, and without taking the pool
offline.
Every allocated block is read, re-encoded at the new parity level, and rewritten;
the extra parity column is stored in space that already exists in the RAIDZ stripe.
.Pp
Because pre-existing blocks and newly written blocks may briefly coexist at
different parity levels, the operation records a per-vdev
.Em parity-epoch table
\(em a list of
.Sy start_txg : Ns Sy width : Ns Sy parity
tuples \(em in the top-level vdev ZAP, and activates the
.Sy raidz_parity_epochs
pool feature.
The RAIDZ reconstruction path selects the layout for each block from its birth
transaction group, so the pool remains importable and fully redundant at every
step, including after a crash mid-operation.
The reshape is transactional: it either
.Sy COMMITTED Ns
s at the new parity level or leaves the pool unchanged
.Pq fail-closed .
.Pp
The operation is refused
.Pq leaving all data intact
if any block cannot be safely re-encoded at the target parity, and it will not
commit while blocks pinned at the old parity remain reachable
.Pq see Sx NOTES .
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--status"
.It Fl -online
Perform the reshape synchronously while keeping all datasets mounted, using
chunked suspend/resume.
Without this option the default synchronous mode briefly unmounts and remounts
the pool's datasets
.Pq auto-quiesce
for the duration of the operation.
.It Fl -async
Start an online reshape in a background kernel thread and return immediately.
Progress is reported with
.Fl -status
and the operation may be stopped with
.Fl -cancel .
.It Fl -status
Report the progress of a background reshape: whether an operation is active or
committed, the target parity, the number of blocks visited, and the residual
count of blocks not yet re-encoded.
.It Fl -cancel
Request cancellation of a background reshape.
.It Fl -target Ar N
Reshape toward parity level
.Ar N
.Pq 2 No or Sy 3
rather than the next level up.
When omitted, the parity is promoted by one level.
.El
.
.Sh NOTES
.Bl -bullet
.It
The pool must contain only RAIDZ top-level vdevs of the source parity level.
The
.Sy raidz_parity_epochs
feature is activated automatically on first use and is required to import the
pool afterward.
.It
Datasets that are busy
.Pq cannot be quiesced
block the default and
.Fl -online
modes; unmount them first with
.Nm zfs Cm unmount Fl a .
.It
Snapshots that pin blocks at the old parity level prevent the operation from
committing.
.Nm zpool Cm reparity Fl -status
reports the residual block count and the number of pinning snapshots; destroy
them and re-run to complete the reshape.
.El
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zpoolconcepts 7 ,
.Xr zpool-attach 8 ,
.Xr zpool-features 7 ,
.Xr zpool-scrub 8 ,
.Xr zpool-status 8
